    "serial": {
        "baud_rate": 57600,
        "comments": "-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.\n\n\nA 3.3V TTL UART is located on the populated 5 pin header J5 in the upper left corner of the main PCB (down is the side with ethernet port, buttons and SIM slots).\n\n{{:media:zyxel:nr7101:red_dsc_3826.jpg?800|NR7101 serial}}\n\nPinout:\n     [o] GND (black)\n     [ ] key - no pin\n     [o] RX (orange)\n     [o] TX (red)\n     [o] 3.3V Vcc (brown)\n\n3.3V should **not** be connected to USB TTL UART adapters, as per [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]], but is available if you want to connect to a Bluetooth TTL UART adapter as shown in the picture.  Bluetooth allows console connections with all gaskets in place, maintaining IP68, but has some obvious security implications. \n\nIt is also possible to route a serial or USB cable through the cable gland used by the ethernet cable, either using 2 thinner cables or a cable with more than 4 pairs. A single multipair round cable is recommended if the router is mounted outdoors.\n\n^ Serial connection parameters\\\\ for ZyXEL NR7101 | 57600, 8N1 |\n",
